  "prompt": "Bug: a user who lacks a permission gets no error message.\n\nRoutes guarded by a permission (declared with require(Perm...), checked by RequirePermission) answer 403 to a user without it, for example POST /api/foods for a user without can_organize. But the 403 carries no message. The frontend only shows an error toast when the response has detail.message, so the user clicks and nothing visible happens.\n\nExpected: every permission-guarded route answers a user without the permission with 403 and a detail in the usual error shape (ErrorResponse), whose message is the existing translation exceptions.permission-denied in the request's language (Accept-Language). In English that is \"You do not have permission to perform this action\".\n\nRequirePermission objects are called with the user and a translator, check(user, translator), where translator is a Translator like the one get_locale_provider returns; inside a route FastAPI must supply both. Without the needed flag it raises an HTTPException with status 403. With it (can_organize, can_manage, can_invite, can_manage_household for GROUP_ORGANIZE, GROUP_MANAGE, GROUP_INVITE, HOUSEHOLD_MANAGE) it returns without error, and Perm.ANY_VALID_USER lets any user through. Which routes need which permission does not change, and users who hold the permission are not refused.\n\nTests: `python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/integration_tests/test_route_permissions.py` for quick loops; the whole backend suite is `python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests` (about 8 minutes).",
  "title": "fix: show an error when a user lacks permission for an action (#8808)",
  "track": "fix",
  "fixCommit": "4b32e54bba05942017f55f004b361b77582d22be",
